{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":4096,\"evidence\":[\"receipt-1\"],\"confidence\":1.0,\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"reason\":\"All assignments satisfy CNF; unsatisfying impossible due to conflicting clauses.\"}","reasoning_content":"We need count of assignments satisfying CNF. 12 variables. Clauses list. Let's enumerate logically. Use brute force mentally? 12 vars => 4096 combos. Might use reasoning. Let's analyze constraints.\n\nClauses:\n1. -7 OR 12\n2. -5 OR 6\n3. -4 OR 8\n4. 3 OR 2\n5. 10 OR 7\n6. 11 OR 5\n7. -2 OR 9\n8. -3 OR 9\n9. -11 OR 6\n10. 1 OR 4\n11. -1 OR 8\n12. -10 OR 12\n\nWe can treat as implications.\n\nRewrite each clause as implication: For clause (a OR b), equivalent to (~a -> b) and (~b -> a). But easier: we can find assignments that violate any clause. Count satisfying = total - unsatisfying. Unsatisfying assignments are those where all clauses false. For clause to be false, both literals must be false. So unsatisfying assignments must satisfy for each clause: literal1 false AND literal2 false.\n\nThus we need assignments where for each clause, both literals false. That gives constraints:\n\n1. -7 false => 7 true. 12 false => 12 false. So 7=1,12=0.\n2. -5 false =>5=1. 6 false =>6=0.\n3. -4 false =>4=1. 8 false =>8=0.\n4. 3 false =>3=0. 2 false =>2=0.\n5. 10 false =>10=0. 7 false =>7=1? Wait clause 5 is (10 OR 7). For false, both 10 false and 7 false. But 7 false means 7=0. Contradiction with clause1 requiring 7=1. So unsatisfying assignments impossible. Thus no assignment can make all clauses false simultaneously. Therefore all assignments satisfy at least one clause? Wait unsatisfying means all clauses false. Since clause5 conflicts with clause1, unsatisfying impossible. Therefore every assignment satisfies CNF. So count = 2^12 = 4096.\n\nCheck if any other contradictions? Clause1 requires 7=1,12=0. Clause5 requires 10=0,7=0. Contradiction on 7. So unsatisfying impossible. Thus all assignments satisfy. So answer 4096.\n\nReturn final."}}],"created":1790955206,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":583,"prompt_tokens":4195,"total_tokens":4778,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-7YtByS75AyevaLCti6cJi87Ox6DqxLzR","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4195,"prompt_ms":514.123,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.12255613825983315,"prompt_per_second":8159.526027818245,"predicted_n":583,"predicted_ms":1830.52,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.1452233676975943,"predicted_per_second":317.9424425846208}}